.\" The manual page of the window the fermix-desktop package installs. build_in_container.sh
.\" compresses it into /usr/share/man/man1/fermix-desktop.1.gz.
.TH FERMIX-DESKTOP 1 "October 2026" "fermix-desktop" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fermix-desktop \- the window of the Fermix assistant
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fermix-desktop
.RB [ \-\-background ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fermix-desktop
is the window of Fermix, a personal assistant that runs as a service of your
own account.
In it you start the service, sign in to a model provider, chat with Fermix or
talk to it by voice, follow its activity and read its log.
.PP
Only one window runs at a time: starting
.B fermix-desktop
again brings the running one forward.
The service itself is
.BR fermix (1),
which this package carries too.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start in the tray, without the window.
This is how the desktop starts Fermix at login when
.I Open at login
is on.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show the options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/fermix\-desktop
The window and the GTK runtime it draws with, private to it.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/fermix\-desktop/copyright
The licences of everything the package carries.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fermix (1)
